note.para:
Some implementations have encoded 8 bit entries with 16 bits allocated, padding the high bits;
                                    this can be detected by comparing the number of entries specified in the LUT Descriptor with the actual Value Length of the LUT Data entry.
                                    The Value Length in bytes should equal the number of entries if bits allocated is 8 (accounting for the need for an additional single padding byte to even length if the number of entries is odd), and be twice as long if bits allocated is 16.
